e  states that his hotels are located in  have seen a lack of growth not just that  but they have topped a list of fastest  shrinking states in the u.s  with new york taking first place and  illinois taking a second place  this is largely due to very high living  expenses  as well as sky high tax rates people  moving out itself is not a negative  as trump's hotels rely on visitors to  the cities as opposed to the people  living there  however as people move out of the states  so do the companies  one of the primary reasons many  companies put up with high taxes and  harsh business policies  in places like california and new york  is because of the talent pool in the  area  but when this is dwindling there is no  reason for them to stay any longer  and a reduction of companies in the area  directly reduces the number of business  travelers coming to the area  business travelers make up 40 of total  hotel guests  and the thing is they likely make for  the majority of the revenue  for instance business travelers only  make up 12  of air travelers however they make up  for 75  of airlines profits this is because they  are more likely to make last-minute  bookings  be willing to pay more for non-stop  flights and of course  book business and first-class seats  similarly  it's likely that business travelers book  last minute hotels  are willing to pay more for hotels  closest central city  and book more expensive rooms themselves  so  though business travelers make up 40  reservations  it's likely they make up for the  majority of the profit and with  businesses leaving the area  this is likely to have a large impact on  the bottom line of airlines  and hotels in the area so a polarization  of many customers  a reduction in quality of customers  experiences a lack of expansion  internationally and domestically  as well as geographical trends have been  the leading factors in the devaluation  of the trump empire  as these account for 1.4 billion in  losses  the last billion comes from the pandemic  which is really quite self-explanatory  most if not all of trump's businesses  are hotels  casinos or country clubs and virtually  no one is traveling or hitting the  casinos  so it's no wonder they're hurting  similarly  the businesses of many country club  members may also be hurting  so they might withdraw from the country  club and  that's how trump lost over half his  wealth he'll likely recover a good  amount as we come out of the pandemic  but if he gets reelected it's likely  that this overall downward trend will  continue  now a lot of people are likely going to  be ecstatic  citing that he deserves to lose his  money for the disservice he has done for  the country  while others will respect him even more  classifying the laws as a noble  sacrifice  from good old donald j trump personally  i don't think we should be particularly  happy at a president's misfortune  but that's just what i think if you guys  like the depth of this analysis  drop a like and consider subscribing to  see more questions logically answered  but until then i'm hari and i'll see you  guys on the next one  you
 

